{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Matrix Transformations Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Transformation matrices from scratch (Python)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rotation_2d(theta):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    c, s = math.cos(theta), math.sin(theta)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [[c, -s], [s, c]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def scaling_2d(sx, sy):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [[sx, 0], [0, sy]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def shearing_2d(kx, ky):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [[1, kx], [ky, 1]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def reflection_x():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [[1, 0], [0, -1]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def reflection_y():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [[-1, 0], [0, 1]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mat_vec_mul(matrix, vector):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sum(matrix[i][j] * vector[j] for j in range(len(vector)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(len(matrix))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mat_mul(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rows_a, cols_b = len(a), len(b[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cols_a = len(a[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        [sum(a[i][k] * b[k][j] for k in range(cols_a)) for j in range(cols_b)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(rows_a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "point = [1.0, 0.0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "angle = math.pi / 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rotated = mat_vec_mul(rotation_2d(angle), point)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Rotate (1,0) by 45 deg: ({rotated[0]:.4f}, {rotated[1]:.4f})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "scaled = mat_vec_mul(scaling_2d(2, 3), [1.0, 1.0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Scale (1,1) by (2,3): ({scaled[0]:.1f}, {scaled[1]:.1f})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sheared = mat_vec_mul(shearing_2d(1, 0), [1.0, 1.0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Shear (1,1) kx=1: ({sheared[0]:.1f}, {sheared[1]:.1f})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "reflected = mat_vec_mul(reflection_y(), [2.0, 1.0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Reflect (2,1) across y: ({reflected[0]:.1f}, {reflected[1]:.1f})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Composition of transformations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "R = rotation_2d(math.pi / 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "S = scaling_2d(2, 0.5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rotate_then_scale = mat_mul(S, R)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "scale_then_rotate = mat_mul(R, S)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "point = [1.0, 0.0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "result1 = mat_vec_mul(rotate_then_scale, point)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "result2 = mat_vec_mul(scale_then_rotate, point)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Rotate 90 then scale: ({result1[0]:.2f}, {result1[1]:.2f})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Scale then rotate 90: ({result2[0]:.2f}, {result2[1]:.2f})\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Same? {result1 == result2}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Eigenvalues from scratch (2x2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For a 2x2 matrix `[[a, b], [c, d]]`, eigenvalues solve the characteristic equation: `lambda^2 - (a+d)*lambda + (ad - bc) = 0`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def eigenvalues_2x2(matrix):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    a, b = matrix[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    c, d = matrix[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    trace = a + d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    det = a * d - b * c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    discriminant = trace ** 2 - 4 * det"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if discriminant < 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        real = trace / 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        imag = (-discriminant) ** 0.5 / 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return (complex(real, imag), complex(real, -imag))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sqrt_disc = discriminant ** 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return ((trace + sqrt_disc) / 2, (trace - sqrt_disc) / 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def eigenvector_2x2(matrix, eigenvalue):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    a, b = matrix[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    c, d = matrix[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if abs(b) > 1e-10:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        v = [b, eigenvalue - a]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    elif abs(c) > 1e-10:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        v = [eigenvalue - d, c]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if abs(a - eigenvalue) < 1e-10:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            v = [1, 0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            v = [0, 1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mag = (v[0] ** 2 + v[1] ** 2) ** 0.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [v[0] / mag, v[1] / mag]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A = [[2, 1], [1, 2]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "vals = eigenvalues_2x2(A)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Matrix: {A}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"Eigenvalues: {vals[0]:.4f}, {vals[1]:.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for val in vals:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    vec = eigenvector_2x2(A, val)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = mat_vec_mul(A, vec)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scaled = [val * vec[0], val * vec[1]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  lambda={val:.1f}, v={[round(x,4) for x in vec]}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"    A@v = {[round(x,4) for x in result]}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"    l*v = {[round(x,4) for x in scaled]}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Determinant as volume scaling factor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def det_2x2(matrix):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return matrix[0][0] * matrix[1][1] - matrix[0][1] * matrix[1][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"det(rotation 45) = {det_2x2(rotation_2d(math.pi/4)):.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"det(scale 2,3)   = {det_2x2(scaling_2d(2, 3)):.1f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"det(shear kx=1)  = {det_2x2(shearing_2d(1, 0)):.1f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"det(reflect y)   = {det_2x2(reflection_y()):.1f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "singular = [[1, 2], [2, 4]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"det(singular)     = {det_2x2(singular):.1f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"Singular: columns are proportional, space collapses to a line.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Apply rotation, scaling, and shearing to a unit square (corners at [0,0], [1,0], [1,1], [0,1]). Print the transformed corners for each. Verify that rotation preserves distances between corners.\n\n2. Find the eigenvalues of the matrix [[4, 2], [1, 3]] by hand using the characteristic equation. Then verify with your from-scratch function and with NumPy.\n\n3. Create a composition of three transformations (rotate 30 degrees, scale by [1.5, 0.8], shear with kx=0.3) and apply it to 8 points arranged in a circle. Print before and after coordinates. Compute the determinant of the composed matrix and verify it equals the product of the individual determinants."
      ]
    }
